Harbor: InternetSetOption accepts INTERNET_OPTION_LISTEN_TIMEOUT (#92).

Option 11 fell through to "Option STUB" and ERROR_INTERNET_INVALID_OPTION. Office sets it on the session before
its account requests and gives up on the request when that fails: signing in ended with error code 12009. The
value is accepted and not used.

Test: WindowsTests/apigaps/run.sh.

--- a/dlls/wininet/internet.c	2026-11-26 16:00:03
+++ b/dlls/wininet/internet.c	2026-11-26 16:00:03
@@ -3687,6 +3687,11 @@
         ret = (res == ERROR_SUCCESS);
         break;
         }
+    case INTERNET_OPTION_LISTEN_TIMEOUT:
+        /* HARBOR HACK: a timeout from the FTP days that nothing here uses. Office sets it before its account
+         * requests and gives up on the request (error 12009) when that fails (#92). */
+        TRACE("INTERNET_OPTION_LISTEN_TIMEOUT: accepted, not used\n");
+        break;
     default:
         FIXME("Option %ld STUB\n",dwOption);
         SetLastError(ERROR_INTERNET_INVALID_OPTION);
